From 306523c2672a26b80a8205787e75c023b39f4538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <abhishek01789@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:58:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/41] Minimize with KWin's Magic Lamp, show taskbar groups in
 a Window View

Magic Lamp: a port of KWin's magiclamp effect. A minimizing window
pours into its taskbar entry, and pours back out on restore. The
shader inverts KWin's per-side formulas per pixel. Duration is KWin's
700 ms times the 0.25 animation factor of this machine.

The compositor now stores org_kde_plasma_window.set_minimized_geometry
in global coordinates and exposes it as window.minimizedGeometry.
Without one, the lamp aims at the cursor, like KWin.

Window View: a helper owns org.kde.KWin.Effect.WindowView1 on the
session bus, so the taskbar shows a group's windows side by side
instead of a text list. It passes the window ids to the config, which
opens the window grid with only those windows, styled like KWin.
